Description: drm: Show each eye of a stereo pair whose outputs can't share a commit
 A stereo pair is presented in one atomic commit, which only works when
 both outputs are on the same GPU. With the outputs on two GPUs, or with
 the partner missing or disabled, presentStereoPair() returned
 InvalidArguments for every frame. Both outputs then never showed a new
 frame, and each failed frame made the compositor render it again and
 re-probe every connector of every GPU, which left the other outputs at
 a fraction of their refresh rate.
 .
 Present such an output on its own instead. Its primary plane already
 reads its own eye from the side by side frame it rendered, so each
 output still shows its eye, only without the shared commit.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: https://github.com/Sparky-OS/kwin/commit/dea37d64fa34ab1abee0870ee7569d7ffd128f90
Forwarded: no
